s/new-york/sullivan-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sullivan County","/arc-plc/new-york/sullivan-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids in Sullivan County came in under 90% of normal for September to October in 37 of the 75 years since 1951. In 2025 that middle ran 161% of normal for April to May and 163% for May to June, then fell to 79% of normal for September to October in 2025. July to August is the wettest pair at 8.74 inches of normal, and January to February is the driest at 5.92 inches.</p>"}
